{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Frequent: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja27'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 27 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Kuruṅgavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Four-horned Antelope </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>7. Abhiṇhajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Frequent: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Nālaṁ kabaḷaṁ padātave, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It’s not enough to give him a morsel, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na ca piṇḍaṁ na kuse na ghaṁsituṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a bite, some grass, or a rubbing-down. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Maññāmi abhiṇhadassanā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I think by seeing the dog often, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nāgo snehamakāsi kukkure”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the elephant grew fond of him. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Abhiṇhajātakaṁ sattamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
